<entity-facade-xml type="seed-initial">
    <!-- Insights P3 (impl-insights P3, §4, F4, F5, F9, F10, F30; design-insights §5): dataset admission. Every business dataset
        (signal business) is read only once admitted (the framework's moqui.report.BusinessDataset; crates/moqui-report/src/business.rs),
        except by its steward, who holds the dataset's update artifact; admission needs the document in a registered DataFeed, its
        index built and Mantle's organization row filter (the ReportScopePolicy MantleOrganization) bound, so each viewer reads
        their own organizations' rows in rows, suggestions, value counts, aggregates and exports alike. The grants below give the
        Insights groups each business dataset's own artifact (view; the steward update, its index#BusinessDataset guard) and its
        documents' DataDocumentUserGroup rows; the owners' report groups are granted below (BOSS_COM_DATASETS, BOSS_CS_DATASETS and
        their documents' rows). Datasets a steward creates are named insights-*: the
        pattern grants the dataset a steward names, never a source under it (an alias of a log index, or of a business document without
        its signal, needs the source's own artifact of its saver and reader: the engine's alias.rs, impl-admin F277). The
        Insights administrator reads no dataset (its business data stays a separate grant). Never grant an Insights group
        org.moqui.report.dataset.* or a DataDocument-by-id or index: dataset: the engine opens those over a business dataset's
        document only to a holder of their update artifact (impl-insights F53, review R1), which would read them unfiltered. -->
    <artifactGroups artifactGroupId="BOSS_INS_DATASETS" description="Insights: the business datasets">
        <artifacts artifactName="org.moqui.report.dataset.mantle-sales-orders" artifactTypeEnumId="AT_SERVICE"/>
        <artifacts artifactName="org.moqui.report.dataset.mantle-sales-items" artifactTypeEnumId="AT_SERVICE"/>
