    <!-- The framework's dataset calcgrid (mr-moqui tools/report/calcgrid.json; docs/tools/Database.md, CalcGrid and access
        profiles): a range of a saved CalcGrid document as a panel's table, read as the viewer under their CalcGrid access.
        The report engine asks the dataset's own artifact and then the service it names, get#CalcFrame, each as the viewer's
        own grant, which the Insights root's grant does not pass (mr-moqui plans/IronCalc-DB2.md CG1.1). Neither is a
        ReportServices operation, so BOSS_INS_REPORT_ENGINE's deny does not reach them, and a plain ALLOW holds; the one it
        asks below them, check#DefinitionRead, is the readers' (BOSS_INS_REPORT_READ, BossSetupData07). It reads no
        index and is not a business dataset (the engine refuses a business dataset that names a service): get#CalcFrame
        checks the document's share and the caller's access profile on each call, so this grant gives no row the reader's
        own profile does not. Each Insights group reads it, as the business datasets above. The panel editor offers the
        dataset's parameters with their choices, each read by the viewer's own grant of its service (mr-moqui
        plans/IronCalc-DB2.md CG4.1): the documents through list#Definitions (BOSS_INS_REPORT_READ), the access profiles
        through get#CalcProfiles, which answers only the profiles the caller holds, so it is here too. -->
    <artifactGroups artifactGroupId="BOSS_INS_CALC_DATASET" description="Insights: the CalcGrid range dataset">
